Notes on a credible moral law

    : see notepad:2026-10-18a,d : all known, possible explanantia for the safehold that hold promise
      of being adapted to account for an explanandum of both safehold and coincidence combined
      lead as such to the same conclusion
        : cf. @ 26.thesis.notes.brec
        ? what of other explanantia?
            : ad `other explanantia` : other than all known, possible explanantia for the safehold
              that hold promise of being adapted to account for an explanandum
              of both safehold and coincidence combined *as such*
                : re `other than (.+) \*as such\*`s see `^*: .+ : ${same}`p
            ? what of the unpromising
                | all known, possible non-null explanantia for an explanandum of safehold
                  and coincidence combined lead to the same conclusion
                    : ad `all.+explanantia` : not only the promising, but also the unpromising
                    go+ with this
              \ |
              \     ?+ how then reconcile ‘promising’ with ‘credible’?
            ?+ what of those for an explanandum of the coincidence alone?
                - the safehold still takes part in that explanandum as a coincider
                ∴ the safehold must still figure in the explanantia
                - yet without an account (in whole or part) for the safehold itself
                    ∵ such an account would not be proper to ‘other explanantia’
                        : re `other explanantia` see `^*: ad \`${same}\``
                    ∵ ‘other explanantia’ alone are being considered here
                ∴ without an account for the safehold’s congruity with the other coinciders
                    ∵ accounting for the safehold’s congruity would account also for its fitness
                        : re `fitness` see `^*\(6\).+highly fit to secure.+long-term survival` @
                          ../20.a_surprising_coincidence.brec : it being so
                        ∵ the congruity inheres in the fitness
                    ∵ accounting for the fitness would account also (in whole or part) for the safehold
                        ∵ the fitness inheres in the safehold
                ∴ only by accounting for the other coinciders’ congruity with the safehold
                ?+ what follows from that?
                    - it begins to feel improbable at the least
            ?+ what of the remainder
        ?+ precisely what qualification, if not ‘credible’, is most apt for the conclusion?
